SPEC = {
 "file":"cover_lek_associate_consultant_data_scientist",
 "label":"L.E.K. Consulting Associate Consultant Data Scientist",
 "paras":[
 r"I am writing to apply for the Associate Consultant (Data Scientist) position in the Digital Data \& AI team at L.E.K. Consulting. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after graduating from Imperial College London, and I work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. I am early in my career, so I am applying at this grade on the strength of what I have owned rather than years served, and I have set out below exactly where my experience of leading others comes from.",

 r"What attracts me most to L.E.K. is that the Digital Data \& AI team sits alongside case teams rather than apart from them, so the analysis has to survive contact with a commercial recommendation. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. I am particularly drawn to shaping the approach to an ambiguous question and helping define standards for model validation, reproducible code and responsible AI use, because those decide whether an analysis can be trusted twice.",

 r"On turning an ambiguous commercial question into a deliverable analytical plan, my clearest example is DS Digital Technology. A pharmaceutical client wanted to know whether their patient-facing AI was safe enough to deploy, which is not a question you can answer as posed. I turned it into a measurable one: a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension safety rubric with red-line rules, agreed with subject-matter experts, which became the client's acceptance standard. I built a Python pipeline calling six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation that produced and scored more than 2,400 responses, co-built a reviewed knowledge graph, and designed blinded paired A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved answer quality. I presented the findings and the limitations to the client.",

 r"On leading and coaching others I want to be precise rather than overstate it. I was team lead on a UCL group project building a clinical NLP pipeline that parses radiology reports into structured features: I set the approach, divided the work, reviewed my teammates' outputs and was accountable for what we delivered, and our fine-tuned PubMedBERT models beat the TF-IDF and kNN baselines. Earlier I was Conference Team Leader at Huawei Connect in Shanghai, leading a team supporting more than 20,000 attendees. What I have not done is coach junior data scientists inside a professional team, and I would be learning that part of the role rather than arriving with it.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I mine large-scale merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python to identify growth and operations drivers that shape UK market-entry and expansion strategy. I also built an AI agent, using Claude Code, that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow; it was adopted by the wider team and partner teams, which is the closest I have come to building something other analysts depend on.",

 r"My MSc dissertation is where the analytical standards come from. I compared logistic regression against three tree ensembles for cardiovascular risk prediction on 458,840 UK Biobank participants, judging them on calibration rather than headline accuracy, then used doubly robust causal forests to estimate individual-level effects. Much of the work was establishing how far the conclusions could be pushed before they broke: overlap weighting, sensitivity analysis including E-values and quantitative bias analysis, and external validation in a second cohort. I reported null results where I found them. On the strategy consulting experience you list as nice to have, I spent a summer at Ipsos Strategy3 shaping the analytical approach for healthcare engagements, structuring 80+ expert interviews into quantitative evidence and building market-sizing models.",

 r"The gaps are the ones you would expect at my stage: my cloud experience is basic on AWS, I have not owned a model deployment in production, and my coaching experience is academic rather than professional. My Python, my SQL, my statistics and my experience designing and defending evaluations of generative AI systems are well established.",

 r"I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship, and I am based in London. I have also applied to the Associate (Data Scientist) role and would be glad to be considered at whichever grade you think fits.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss where my experience sits against this role.",
 ]
}
